From: Rob Lymm <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: send the context rollover packet

The dummy set-constant that makes the shader front end roll its context has
sat behind #if 0 since this driver was written, and no longer compiled: the
register it names was renamed and the CP_REG helper is gone. Qualcomm's
driver sends this packet after every A3XX submission.

The shader front end is one of the blocks left busy when this GPU locks up
under many small draws.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-09-20 06:50:51.809313661 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-09-20 06:50:51.809253769 +0100
@@ -81,12 +81,15 @@
 	OUT_RING(ring, rbmemptr(ring, fence));
 	OUT_RING(ring, submit->seqno);
 
-#if 0
-	/* Dummy set-constant to trigger context rollover */
+	/*
+	 * Dummy set-constant to trigger context rollover. Qualcomm's driver
+	 * sends this after every A3XX submission; upstream has carried it
+	 * disabled since this driver was written.
+	 */
 	OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
-	OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A3XX_HLSQ_CL_KERNEL_GROUP_X_REG));
+	OUT_RING(ring, (0x4 << 16) |
+		(REG_A3XX_HLSQ_CL_KERNEL_GROUP(0) - 0x2000));
 	OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
-#endif
 
 	adreno_flush(gpu, ring, REG_AXXX_CP_RB_WPTR);
 }
